  /// resource or the Journey resource to define a custom quiet time for the
  /// campaign or journey.
  pub quiet_time: QuietTime? = None
  /// The default sending limits for journeys in the application. These limits
  /// apply to each journey for the application but can be overridden, on a
  /// per journey basis, with the JourneyLimits resource.
  pub journey_limits: ApplicationSettingsJourneyLimits? = None
}

/// Specifies the configuration and other settings for a campaign.
pub struct WriteCampaignRequest {
  /// An array of requests that defines additional treatments for the
  /// campaign, in addition to the default treatment for the campaign.
  pub additional_treatments: List[WriteTreatmentResource]? = None
  /// The delivery configuration settings for sending the campaign through a
  /// custom channel. This object is required if the MessageConfiguration
  /// object for the campaign specifies a CustomMessage object.
  pub custom_delivery_configuration: CustomDeliveryConfiguration? = None
  /// A custom description of the campaign.
  pub description: Str? = None
  /// The allocated percentage of users (segment members) who shouldn't
  /// receive messages from the campaign.
  pub holdout_percent: Int? = None
  /// The settings for the AWS Lambda function to invoke as a code hook for
  /// the campaign. You can use this hook to customize the segment that's used
  /// by the campaign.
  pub hook: CampaignHook? = None
  /// Specifies whether to pause the campaign. A paused campaign doesn't run
  /// unless you resume it by changing this value to false.
  pub is_paused: Bool? = None
  /// The messaging limits for the campaign.
  pub limits: CampaignLimits? = None
  /// The message configuration settings for the campaign.
  pub message_configuration: MessageConfiguration? = None
  /// A custom name for the campaign.
  pub name: Str? = None
  /// The schedule settings for the campaign.
  pub schedule: Schedule? = None
  /// The unique identifier for the segment to associate with the campaign.
  pub segment_id: Str? = None
  /// The version of the segment to associate with the campaign.
  pub segment_version: Int? = None
  /// As of 22-05-2023 tags has been deprecated for update operations. After
  /// this date any value in tags is not processed and an error code is not
  /// returned. To manage tags we recommend using either Tags in the API
  /// Reference for Amazon Pinpoint , resourcegroupstaggingapi commands in the
  /// AWS Command Line Interface Documentation or resourcegroupstaggingapi in
  /// the AWS SDK . (Deprecated) A string-to-string map of key-value pairs
  /// that defines the tags to associate with the campaign. Each tag consists
  /// of a required tag key and an associated tag value.
  pub tags: Map[Str, Str]? = None
  /// The message template to use for the campaign.
  pub template_configuration: TemplateConfiguration? = None
  /// A custom description of the default treatment for the campaign.
  pub treatment_description: Str? = None
  /// A custom name of the default treatment for the campaign, if the campaign
  /// has multiple treatments. A treatment is a variation of a campaign that's
  /// used for A/B testing.
  pub treatment_name: Str? = None
  /// Defines the priority of the campaign, used to decide the order of
  /// messages displayed to user if there are multiple messages scheduled to
  /// be displayed at the same moment.
  pub priority: Int? = None
}

/// Specifies the Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of an event stream to publish
/// events to and the AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) role to use
/// when publishing those events.
pub struct WriteEventStream {
  /// The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the Amazon Kinesis data stream or
  /// Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream that you want to publish
  /// event data to. For a Kinesis data stream, the ARN format is:
  /// arn:aws:kinesis: region : account-id :stream/ stream_name For a Kinesis
  /// Data Firehose delivery stream, the ARN format is: arn:aws:firehose:
  /// region : account-id :deliverystream/ stream_name
  pub destination_stream_arn: Str? = None
  /// The AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) role that authorizes Amazon
  /// Pinpoint to publish event data to the stream in your AWS account.
  pub role_arn: Str? = None
}

/// Specifies the configuration and other settings for a journey.
pub struct WriteJourneyRequest {
  /// A map that contains a set of Activity objects, one object for each
  /// activity in the journey. For each Activity object, the key is the unique
  /// identifier (string) for an activity and the value is the settings for
  /// the activity. An activity identifier can contain a maximum of 100
  /// characters. The characters must be alphanumeric characters.
  pub activities: Map[Str, Activity]? = None
  /// The date, in ISO 8601 format, when the journey was created.
  pub creation_date: Str? = None
  /// The date, in ISO 8601 format, when the journey was last modified.
  pub last_modified_date: Str? = None
  /// The messaging and entry limits for the journey.
  pub limits: JourneyLimits? = None
  /// Specifies whether the journey's scheduled start and end times use each
  /// participant's local time. To base the schedule on each participant's
  /// local time, set this value to true.
  pub local_time: Bool? = None
  /// The name of the journey. A journey name can contain a maximum of 150
  /// characters. The characters can be alphanumeric characters or symbols,
  /// such as underscores (_) or hyphens (-). A journey name can't contain any
  /// spaces.
  pub name: Str? = None
  /// The quiet time settings for the journey. Quiet time is a specific time
  /// range when a journey doesn't send messages to participants, if all the
  /// following conditions are met: The EndpointDemographic.Timezone property
  /// of the endpoint for the participant is set to a valid value. The current
  /// time in the participant's time zone is later than or equal to the time
  /// specified by the QuietTime.Start property for the journey. The current
  /// time in the participant's time zone is earlier than or equal to the time
  /// specified by the QuietTime.End property for the journey. If any of the
  /// preceding conditions isn't met, the participant will receive messages
  /// from the journey, even if quiet time is enabled.
  pub quiet_time: QuietTime? = None
  /// The frequency with which Amazon Pinpoint evaluates segment and event
  /// data for the journey, as a duration in ISO 8601 format.
  pub refresh_frequency: Str? = None
  /// The schedule settings for the journey.
  pub schedule: JourneySchedule? = None
  /// The unique identifier for the first activity in the journey. The
  /// identifier for this activity can contain a maximum of 128 characters.
  /// The characters must be alphanumeric characters.
  pub start_activity: Str? = None
  /// The segment that defines which users are participants in the journey.
  pub start_condition: StartCondition? = None
  /// The status of the journey. Valid values are: DRAFT - Saves the journey
  /// and doesn't publish it. ACTIVE - Saves and publishes the journey.
  /// Depending on the journey's schedule, the journey starts running
  /// immediately or at the scheduled start time. If a journey's status is
  /// ACTIVE, you can't add, change, or remove activities from it. PAUSED,
  /// CANCELLED, COMPLETED, and CLOSED states are not supported in requests to
  /// create or update a journey. To cancel, pause, or resume a journey, use
  /// the Journey State resource.
  pub state: State? = None
  /// Specifies whether endpoints in quiet hours should enter a wait till the
  /// end of their quiet hours.
  pub wait_for_quiet_time: Bool? = None
  /// Indicates whether the journey participants should be refreshed when a
  /// segment is updated.
  pub refresh_on_segment_update: Bool? = None
  /// The channel-specific configurations for the journey.
  pub journey_channel_settings: JourneyChannelSettings? = None
  /// Indicates if journey has Advance Quiet Time enabled. This flag should be
  /// set to true in order to allow using OpenHours and ClosedDays.
  pub sending_schedule: Bool? = None
  /// The time when journey allow to send messages. QuietTime should be
  /// configured first and SendingSchedule should be set to true.
  pub open_hours: OpenHours? = None
  /// The time when journey will stop sending messages. QuietTime should be
  /// configured first and SendingSchedule should be set to true.
  pub closed_days: ClosedDays? = None
  /// An array of time zone estimation methods, if any, to use for determining
  /// an Endpoints time zone if the Endpoint does not have a value for the
  /// Demographic.Timezone attribute. PHONE_NUMBER - A time zone is determined
  /// based on the Endpoint.Address and Endpoint.Location.Country. POSTAL_CODE
  /// - A time zone is determined based on the Endpoint.Location.PostalCode
  /// and Endpoint.Location.Country. POSTAL_CODE detection is only supported
  /// in the United States, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, Canada,
  /// France, Italy, Spain, Germany and in regions where Amazon Pinpoint is
  /// available.
  pub timezone_estimation_methods: List[TimezoneEstimationMethodsElement]? = None
}

/// Specifies the configuration, dimension, and other settings for a
/// segment. A WriteSegmentRequest object can include a Dimensions object or
/// a SegmentGroups object, but not both.
pub struct WriteSegmentRequest {
  /// The criteria that define the dimensions for the segment.
  pub dimensions: SegmentDimensions? = None
  /// The name of the segment.
  pub name: Str? = None
  /// The segment group to use and the dimensions to apply to the group's base
  /// segments in order to build the segment. A segment group can consist of
  /// zero or more base segments. Your request can include only one segment
  /// group.
  pub segment_groups: SegmentGroupList? = None
  /// As of 22-05-2023 tags has been deprecated for update operations. After
  /// this date any value in tags is not processed and an error code is not
  /// returned. To manage tags we recommend using either Tags in the API
  /// Reference for Amazon Pinpoint , resourcegroupstaggingapi commands in the
  /// AWS Command Line Interface Documentation or resourcegroupstaggingapi in
  /// the AWS SDK . (Deprecated) A string-to-string map of key-value pairs
  /// that defines the tags to associate with the segment. Each tag consists
  /// of a required tag key and an associated tag value.
  pub tags: Map[Str, Str]? = None
}

/// Specifies the settings for a campaign treatment. A treatment is a
/// variation of a campaign that's used for A/B testing of a campaign.
pub struct WriteTreatmentResource {
  /// The delivery configuration settings for sending the treatment through a
  /// custom channel. This object is required if the MessageConfiguration
  /// object for the treatment specifies a CustomMessage object.
  pub custom_delivery_configuration: CustomDeliveryConfiguration? = None
  /// The message configuration settings for the treatment.
  pub message_configuration: MessageConfiguration? = None
  /// The schedule settings for the treatment.
  pub schedule: Schedule? = None
  /// The allocated percentage of users (segment members) to send the
  /// treatment to.
  pub size_percent: Int? = None
  /// The message template to use for the treatment.
  pub template_configuration: TemplateConfiguration? = None
  /// A custom description of the treatment.
  pub treatment_description: Str? = None
  /// A custom name for the treatment.
  pub treatment_name: Str? = None
}

pub enum EndpointTypesElement: Str {
  Push = "PUSH"
  Gcm = "GCM"
  Apns = "APNS"
  ApnsSandbox = "APNS_SANDBOX"
  ApnsVoip = "APNS_VOIP"
  ApnsVoipSandbox = "APNS_VOIP_SANDBOX"
  Adm = "ADM"
  Sms = "SMS"
  Voice = "VOICE"
  Email = "EMAIL"
  Baidu = "BAIDU"
  Custom = "CUSTOM"
  InApp = "IN_APP"
  Unknown(value: Str)
}

pub enum TimezoneEstimationMethodsElement: Str {
  PhoneNumber = "PHONE_NUMBER"
  PostalCode = "POSTAL_CODE"
  Unknown(value: Str)
}
